-- Step 26: supplier payments, advances and withholding challans.
-- track: B
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/*/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle.
-- Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- A payment goes out of a cash or bank account to one supplier. It is a draft the app writes,
-- with what it settles of which posted bills. Posting it is one act of the database,
-- app.post_supplier_payment:
--
--   debit   Trade payables            what it settles of the supplier's bills
--   debit   Advances to suppliers     whatever is left over: an advance
--   credit  the cash or bank account  the rupees that went out
--
-- An advance is set against a later bill with app.apply_supplier_advance (debit Trade payables,
-- credit Advances to suppliers), and a payment entered by mistake is taken back with
-- app.cancel_supplier_payment, which posts the opposite of everything it posted. A bill is
-- never paid more than is owed on it: what a bill is owed is what Step 25 left owed to the
-- supplier after tax was withheld, less what posted payments have settled of it.
--
-- A payment to a supplier abroad records the currency and how much of it the rupees bought,
-- for the record only. The books hold the rupees actually paid, and an advance is never
-- revalued (the founder's decision, 2026-11-15); bills are in rupees, so setting an advance
-- against a bill leaves no exchange difference.
--
-- Tax withheld on bills (Step 25) is paid to the government under a challan, recorded with
-- app.record_withholding_challan: debit the withholding payable account of that kind, credit
-- the cash or bank account. A challan pays whole withholding entries, each once.
--
-- The owner and an accountant pay suppliers and record challans; the auditor reads. The app's
-- role cannot write a payment's status, number or journal, an advance set against a bill, or
-- anything of a challan.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE200 to SE299 (docs/PARALLEL.md); Step 30 used SE200
-- to SE210, Step 24 SE211 to SE222 and Step 25 SE223 to SE234:
--   SE235  no such supplier payment in this company (or outside the member's branches)
--   SE236  the payment is not in the state this needs
--   SE237  a posted payment is never changed or removed
--   SE238  what a payment settles is written only while it is a draft, and names a posted bill
--          of the payment's supplier and branch, dated on or before the payment
--   SE239  more set against a bill than is still owed on it
--   SE240  more set against bills than the payment, or than is left of the advance
--   SE241  the money leaves a cash or bank account that is in use
--   SE242  a date that has not come yet, is no day on the calendar, or is before what it follows
--   SE243  a challan pays whole withholding entries of its own kind, each once
--   SE244  nothing to set against a bill, or the same bill twice
--   SE245  a foreign currency is one of the company's own, other than the one it keeps its books in
-- SE219 (purchase documents are written in read committed transactions) is Step 24's, used again.

